{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_jv6k3iep2n75s47iq4mabmyrwq2u7v7ks7rmg5o7i6k42tq6siqa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — **ALL CHECKS PASSED**. Two real divergences found and fixed.\n\n## Bugs found & fixed in the Rust\n\n**1. `INT_MIN / -1` did not trap** (`divide_operation`, `modulo_operation`)\n\n| input | C | Rust before | Rust after |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `divide_operation(INT_MIN,-1,0)` | `SIGFPE` (8) | returned `INT_MIN` | `SIGFPE` (8) |\n| `modulo_operation(INT_MIN,-1,0)` | `SIGFPE` (8) | returned `0` | `SIGFPE` (8) |\n| `mathop(INT_MIN,-1,3,1)` | `SIGFPE` (8) | returned a value | `SIGFPE` (8) |\n\nReachable from `mathop` — the *only* function in `lib.h` (`param3=3` selects `OP_DIVIDE`). Found when the randomized Phase B sweep killed the harness. `wrapping_div` returns silently; plain `/` panics → `SIGABRT` (6). Fixed with a `cdq; idiv` inline-asm helper, so Rust emits the same instruction the C compiler does.\n\n**2. NULL out-params aborted instead of segfaulting** — *release looked fine; only `dev` diverged*\n\n`perform_computation_with_history(1,2,1,NULL,&cnt)`: C → `SIGSEGV` (11), Rust dev → `SIGABRT` (6). With `debug-assertions = on`, rustc's null-deref UB check fires before the hardware fault and panics across the `extern \"C\"` boundary. `read_volatile`/`write_volatile` carry the *same* check and did not help — fixed with single-`mov` inline asm.\n\n**3. Harness bug worth flagging:** `cargo test` does **not** re-emit the `cdylib`, so tests silently ran against a stale `.so` (this initially masked bug 2). The harness now refuses to run if `libmathop_lib.so` is older than `src/lib.rs`.\n\n## Coverage\n\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — 12/12 symbols, `nm -D` diff **empty**; `ldd -r` fully resolves; no stubs.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 25/25 rows pass, seeded-random. Includes exhaustive 256-value `char` sweep, 4693 lockstep `mathop` calls with **byte-identical stdout**, raw-byte `ComputationResult` image compares, and the composed `select_operation` → pointer → `perform_computation_with_history` pipeline.\n- `ERRORS.md` — 22/22 rows pass, incl. out-of-range enums, negative/`INT_MAX` `calloc` counts, the `<10` bound, the count-reset-on-NULL quirk, the dead validation store, and a controlled out-of-bounds write from a negative count. The two crashing rows use fork-based signal comparison with a benign control case so they can't pass vacuously.\n- All of the above under **4 configurations** (release/debug × default/`--no-default-features`); no `[features]` table exists, so that is the complete set. `verify.sh` automates the whole gate.\n- A mutation check (`op*10` → `op*11`) was caught by 2 tests, confirming the suite isn't vacuous. `c_src/` unmodified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2318,"cache_read_input_tokens":134321,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2318,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"32899e14-d317-492d-8276-b577aad81acb","uuid":"43390561-fcb4-4483-b18d-770f5e8128a9","timestamp":"2026-09-05T15:16:40.017Z"}
